--TEST--
an expression `catch` arm names one class, and a union is refused asking for a second arm — `rule:expressions/catch-expression`'s E0245
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:expressions/catch-expression`: an arm's `( Type $var? )` is the block form's, resolved and
// refused the same way — the binding carries one static type, so a union has
// no type to give it. Only the fix differs: another arm, where the block
// form asks for another clause.
uint $len = Core\Str::length("hi") catch (RuntimeError|LogicError $e) => Core\Str::length("");
echo $len, "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0245]: a `catch` clause names one class
%A
  = help: write one `catch` arm per class, each with its own variable name, or one arm naming a class they all extend
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
